# Weight profile nemotron-bolt-exl3-4.0: NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Bolt 74B-A9B in our EXL3 pack at 4.0 bpw (ENG-337),
# head 6 bits (exllamav3 1.6.2 with the Puzzle/Bolt patch, mul1 codebook; 40.01 GB, the RADIO tower kept in BF16 and
# not loaded), converted from nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-74B-A9B-BF16 at revision bca0a8cb. The pack is in a
# public Hugging Face repository. Measured 2026-10-15 against BF16 (8 wikitext rows x 1,024): KL 0.034, top-1 92.7 %;
# decode 38.4 tok/s from its graph (one CTA a row, measured before the rows path). NVIDIA's LiLiCorr drafter and the
# lookup draft, cut by StairCut (no price file yet: the cut learns its prices online).
# Switch with ops/use-profile.sh nemotron-bolt-exl3-4.0.
QSE_NH_MODEL=nemotron-3.5-bolt-74b-a9b
QSE_NH_VARIANT=bolt-exl3-4.0
QSE_WEIGHTS_GB=40.01
MAX_LEN=262144
# MemAvailable (GiB) a start needs: the weights (36.18 allocated, measured), the engine and its graphs, the
# allocator, the prefill workspace, three slots' KV, LiLiCorr (1.32 allocated, measured) and the 15 GiB floor
QSE_MEM_NEED_GIB=66
# the engine's limits. Ceiling: the weights (36.18) + the runtime (an estimate of 4 until measured) + the KV of
# three slots at 262,144 tokens (6) + LiLiCorr (1.32); peak: the ceiling + the prefill workspace (an estimate of 4)
MEM_CEILING_GIB=48
MEM_PEAK_GIB=52
# NVIDIA's LiLiCorr drafter (SPD-123): a draft head of the tree drafter beside the lookup, the IQ2 profile's asset
QSE_NH_HEAD=lilicorr
QSE_NH_LILICORR=${HOME}/models/nemotron-3.5-bolt-lilicorr
. "${REPO}/ops/profiles/_nemotron.env"
QSE_WEIGHTS_HF=0xBakeer/TandemLLM-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-74B-A9B-EXL3-4.0
QSE_WEIGHTS_REVISION=9fbf616ea3bd808f09e3470bb960a12f63b66034
# LiLiCorr: the registry entry's asset (models/nemotron-3.5-bolt-74b-a9b/model.yaml), fetched when missing
QSE_ASSETS="${QSE_NH_LILICORR}/model.safetensors"
